        "id": 14410,
        "name": "Anestis",
        "username": "Anestis",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/ed8c4c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-08T02:14:04.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hi,</p><p>Just seeking clarification on one fo the Wager Matser's cards (which I can't remember the name of off the top of my head).</p><p>The card reverses the Hero turn order, so that it becomes:</p><ul>\n<li>End of Turn</li>\n<li>Draw</li>\n<li>Power</li>\n<li>Play</li>\n<li>Sart</li>\n</ul><p>Now, in my view this means the Hero\\'s never get a turn and the Villain just keeps playing, because of End of Turn.</p><p>My friend interprest it differently saying that It'[s just Power, Play and Draw that are reversed.</p><p>Again, I don't have the card in front of me so I can't qote it verbatim. &nbsp;We only played Wager Master once, and we won in the first turn by all the heros having even number of hitpoints.</p><p><span>Anestis.</span></p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:46:29.696Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
